From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:40:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8015: Model the PCIe clocks as clock
 gates

The T8015 PMGR exposes pcie_ref and pcie_aux as clock gates that the
PCIe controller drives itself, but t8015-pmgr.dtsi describes them as
power domains. t8010-pmgr.dtsi already uses the clock-gate model for
the same two gates.

Drop the power-domain and reset cells from ps_pcie_ref and ps_pcie_aux,
make them clock controllers with apple,clock-gate-only, and mark ps_pcie
with apple,manual-pm so the PCIe driver owns the power-up sequence,
matching the A10.

This is not inert on boards that leave PCIe disabled. Until the apcie
node is enabled, pcie_ref and pcie_aux have no consumer and no
CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, so clk_disable_unused gates them at late init if
firmware left them on, and ps_pcie no longer keeps them in step with
its own genpd state. It lands with the h9p T8015 match data, and the
boot test reports 0x80148, 0x80320 and 0x80318 before and after.

Signed-off-by: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-pmgr.dtsi | 17 ++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-pmgr.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-pmgr.dtsi
index 1d8da9c..480e54c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-pmgr.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-pmgr.dtsi
@@ -129,12 +129,13 @@
 		apple,always-on; /* Core device */
 	};
 
-	ps_pcie_ref: power-controller@80148 {
+	ps_pcie_ref: clock-controller@80148 {
 		compatible = "apple,t8015-pmgr-pwrstate", "apple,pmgr-pwrstate";
 		reg = <0x80148 4>;
-		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
-		#reset-cells = <0>;
+		#clock-cells = <0>;
 		label = "pcie_ref";
+		apple,clock-gate-only;
+		apple,manual-pm;
 	};
 
 	ps_mca0: power-controller@80170 {
@@ -658,15 +659,17 @@
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 		label = "pcie";
-		power-domains = <&ps_pcie_aux>, <&ps_pcie_direct>, <&ps_pcie_ref>;
+		power-domains = <&ps_pcie_direct>;
+		apple,manual-pm;
 	};
 
-	ps_pcie_aux: power-controller@80320 {
+	ps_pcie_aux: clock-controller@80320 {
 		compatible = "apple,t8015-pmgr-pwrstate", "apple,pmgr-pwrstate";
 		reg = <0x80320 4>;
-		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
-		#reset-cells = <0>;
+		#clock-cells = <0>;
 		label = "pcie_aux";
+		apple,clock-gate-only;
+		apple,manual-pm;
 	};
 
 	ps_vdec0: power-controller@80388 {
